# Files currently over the size limit, frozen at their present length.
#
# Scope is verify_code_size.py's, not "shell": linux/scripts, linux/host-config,
# docs/scripts and linux/llm-stack by *.sh/*.py, plus the Dockerfile* at the top of
# linux/. Seven of the rows below are llm-stack, in scope since EX1 (2026-09-07).
#
# Format: <path> | <lines> | <reason>
#
# Same four-way contract as function-size.allow: growth, a new offender, an
# unrecorded shrink and a stale entry all fail. Shrinking a file means updating
# its number here; deleting the line once it drops under the limit.
#
# The refactor entries live in docs/refactoring-backlog.md F2.

# --- EX1 2026-09-07: linux/llm-stack enters the scan set. These 47 rows are the
# territory the extent gates could never see; every one was read and given a
# verdict in the same wave that widened SCAN, so none is a bare baseline. 34 of
# them say DEBT and name their seam -- that is the honest state of a benchmark
# harness nobody had reviewed for shape. docs/refactoring-backlog.md EX1
linux/Dockerfile.media | 910 | Adjacent core copies share their unchanged pre-RUN closure; the standalone logger is carried for partial media rebuilds. Previous review: 911 -> 912 on 2026-10-18: the ORT GPU RUN mounts linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime again, for the CUDA cstdint patch. PRIOR: 908 -> 911 on 2026-10-17: the hub sccache build -- ENABLE_SCCACHE_RUST/CUDA default 1, and ENABLE_SCCACHE_HIP, its own switch, as an ARG and in the ENV block. PRIOR: 879 -> 908 on 2026-10-17: the shared S3 level -- each of the 14 sccache RUNs gains `--mount=type=secret,id=sccache_s3,required=false` and a closing `bash /opt/scripts/core/sccache-s3-level.sh drain`, and the Arm NN RUN, which mounts no 01-core, the library bind. PRIOR: 880 -> 879 on 2026-10-13: CON95 -- the ORT GPU RUN loses the linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime mount, since v1.31.0 carries upstream's GCC 16 epilogue fix and the patch is gone. PRIOR: 877 -> 880 on 2026-10-13: the shared wasm cache is stamped only once it holds a *.wasm (a non-amd64 target skips the wasm step with rc 0), an elif arm and its one-line why. PRIOR: 873 -> 877 on 2026-10-09: CON75/CON79 1b -- FT_TORCH_TWIN as an ARG in the app-wheelhouse stage (exported to build-app-wheelhouse.sh) and in the final stage, whose free-threaded-store.sh expects the riscv64 torch twin while it is 1, each behind a one-line why. PRIOR: 870 -> 873 on 2026-10-08: CON79 -- the pyav RUN bind-mounts the chain ORT and puts its lib on LD_LIBRARY_PATH behind a one-line why, so the cp314t proof can load libavfilter. PRIOR: 864 -> 870 on 2026-10-07: CON79 4 -- the one twin table both lanes read (03-media/free-threaded-twins.txt) is bind-mounted per file beside free-threaded-wheels.sh into the same six twin RUNs, one line each. PRIOR: 842 -> 864 on 2026-10-07: the cp314t twins -- the free-threaded library and helper bind-mounted per file into the six RUNs that build or store a twin, the uv cache on the ORT cpu and TVM RUNs, the three twin COPYs into final, and its --free-threaded repair, verify and store steps. PRIOR: 841 -> 842 on 2026-10-02: CON42 -- the GCC-16 epilogue-scalars patch bind-mounted per file (linux/scripts/patches/onnxruntime) into the cpu-verify RUN. PRIOR: 814 -> 841 on 2026-10-01: CON42 -- the gated deepstream stage (FROM gstreamer, one RUN, empty unless ENABLE_DEEPSTREAM=true) and its ccache/sccache mounts, and its COPY at the end of final. PRIOR: 1248 -> 814 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 1246 -> 1248 on 2026-09-23: the chain-wheel manifest follow step of the ORT census. PRIOR: 1241 -> 1246 on 2026-09-23: G2 (03-media/ort-provenance.sh, the shared ORT build gate) is mounted per file into its five consumer RUNs (opencv x2, ffmpeg, gstreamer, the genai verify RUN), one line each. PRIOR: 1236 -> 1241 on 2026-09-23: the genai verify RUN mounts and runs verify-genai-ort.sh (GenAI's chain-ORT proof) behind a 2-line why. PRIOR: 1162 -> 1175 on 2026-09-10: TWO sessions fixed the same bug the same day and the merge keeps both halves -- their measured failure story (a native arm64 host resolved every unqualified name to :amd64, binutils:amd64 replaced the aarch64 assembler and `as -EL` failed) with their build_arch_oci fallback, routed through AS1's ubuntu_arch_uses_ports table so the host and target stanzas cannot answer 'which archive' differently. Neither side's count survived (1174 vs 1170); 1175 is measured.
linux/scripts/06-packaging/smoke-runtime-image.sh | 2751 | 2768 -> 2770 on 2026-10-21: CON31 -- the source line and main() call of check-gpu-runtime.sh, which holds the ROCm and TensorRT runtime gates. PRIOR: 2754 -> 2768 on 2026-10-20: CON129's gtk4-dev contract row -- its symptom, the probe's FACT line, _consumer_gtk4_verdict and its dispatch arm (+14). PRIOR: 2751 -> 2754 on 2026-10-13: CON96 review -- check_android_abi fails an amd64 image whose Android payload is off (the Android lane builds only there). PRIOR: 2732 -> 2751 on 2026-10-13: CON96 -- the android-home verdict fails a payload-off image that still sets ANDROID_HOME, and check_android_abi skips a payload-off image but fails one whose /opt/android holds objects (+19). PRIOR: 2713 -> 2732 on 2026-10-11: CON42 — the blacklist probe scans a GPU-less nvidia image with the CUDA driver stubs and reports DeepStream's documented UCX plugin (+19). PRIOR: 2659 -> 2713 on 2026-10-09: CON83's lint-tools and uv-cache-seed contract rows -- their symptoms, probe facts, _rt_tool_pin and the two verdict functions (+54). PRIOR: 2657 -> 2659 on 2026-10-07: the FT-STORE gate, two lines (its source and its main() call); its probe and verdicts live in check-free-threaded-wheels.sh. PRIOR: 2648 -> 2657 on 2026-10-07: the free-threaded-python row proves the toolchain's source build (the -build FACT and its verdict arm), and the tree-arch resolver relocates the per-arch /opt/python-cross-ft COPY source. PRIOR: 2626 -> 2648 on 2026-10-06: CON66's free-threaded-python row. PRIOR: 2596 -> 2626 on 2026-10-06: CON65's cargo-qa-tools row (probe, verdict, symptom, exemption). PRIOR: 2592 -> 2596 on 2026-10-01: CON48's boot probe checks the Vulkan variables stay on /opt/vulkan/active (vkadd/vkarch), stacked on CON50's chrome and android-emulator consumer-contract rows -- the _consumer_test_runtimes_probe fragment (split out so _consumer_contract_probe stays under 80 lines), the two verdicts, their symptoms and three exemption arms: the image's browser must render headless as uid 1001 and the amd64 emulator must run at its pins. PRIOR: 2377 -> 2489 on 2026-10-01: three gates for the :latest rebuild -- _gst_check_blacklist (the plugin-health check now FAILS on an undocumented blacklisted plugin: libgstvalidatessim.so sat in the registry blacklist with no scanner line, CON47) and check_gst_validate_ssim (the override still works under gst-validate on amd64); check_no_libunwind_closure (no shipped file under /opt or /usr/local needs libunwind.so.8, the std::call_once segfault); check_lavapipe_subgroup (LP_NATIVE_VECTOR_WIDTH=256 and lavapipe subgroupSize 8, CON44). PRIOR: 2354 -> 2377 on 2026-10-01: CON42 check_deepstream -- a DeepStream tree only in an nvidia image, and its closure/one-GStreamer/registration gates re-run in the shipped image. PRIOR: 2644 -> 2354 on 2026-09-30: comment sweep. PRIOR: 2612 -> 2644 on 2026-09-30: CON41 -- check_vulkan_loader's probe also lists the instance extensions, and _vk_wsi_verdict fails any arch whose loader lacks VK_KHR_surface or the xcb/xlib/wayland surfaces (arm64 and riscv64 shipped without all three). 2605 -> 2612 on 2026-09-23: the compiler battery's sanitizer case -- -fsanitize=address,undefined over the header abseil includes, libasan+libubsan NEEDED, and the binary RUN only where host == target (SAN_RUN), because qemu-user cannot host ASan/LSan. 2595 -> 2605 on 2026-09-23: _pkg_count, the one flavour-aware name match ARCH-PARITY and VENV-SET share -- the torch-stage ORT census now purges the app lock's PyPI onnxruntime-genai, which on nvidia was the only dist spelled that way (the chain's is onnxruntime-genai-cuda / -trt-rtx), so both gates count any GenAI flavour as the GenAI and every other name stays exact. 2570 -> 2595 on 2026-09-23: G1's check_ort_census (SHIPPED-TRUTH E, the ORT census run in-image; its facts and verdicts live in check-ort-provenance.sh, which this file sources) and its main() call. 2502 -> 2570 on 2026-09-23: G3's ort-crate-env consumer-contract row -- the probe fragment _consumer_ort_env_probe (split out so _consumer_contract_probe stays under 80 lines), the _consumer_ort_env_problem/_verdict pair and the row's symptom: ort-sys must link the chain ORT dynamically with pyke's download disarmed, and load-dynamic must open the chain file. PRIOR: 2454 -> 2498 on 2026-09-21/22 with the arm64 GPU runtime lane (7cf92025: the torch.version.cuda / CUDAExecutionProvider gates and the GPU-aware parity), recorded here late; 2498 -> 2502 on 2026-09-22: the ARCH-PARITY probe reports ENABLE_AMD and _parity_ort_flavor gets its rocm arm (onnxruntime_migraphx), without which the rocm wrapper could never pass its smoke. 2449 -> 2454 on 2026-09-20: the ADV/HAVE probes for PYTORCH_VERSION and TORCHVISION_VERSION, which moved the torch pair into the advertised-vs-actual gate when Dockerfile.torch started advertising them. PRIOR: 2433 -> 2449 on 2026-09-10: the consumer contract now READS the payload-off marker instead of judging an image for an SDK its build host could not install: one FACT line in the probe, a marker-first arm in _consumer_android_verdict, and the SKIP arm the loud unknown-verb default demands. 2387 -> 2433 on 2026-09-07: R1.1, the runtime-side ldd walk over /usr/local/llvm-target/bin -- the sdk stage checks NEEDED against the BUILDER's ldconfig cache, which is how liblldb shipped 3 unstartable binaries of amd64's 142. 2336 -> 2387 on 2026-09-07: VK3's toolset ratchet -- the twenty required tool names, the per-arch frozen floors (_VK_TOOLSET_FROZEN) and _vk_floor_verdict, which is the assertion that 2-of-52 could never have survived. F2 reviewed 2026-09-04 — the backlog names this as the one to split if any gets split; the review says NO. 91 functions -- 45 check_*/_probe_* assertions plus the probe-and-verdict layer they share -- over ONE image through ONE _rt_run, driven by one main(). (This row said "63 functions, all of them check_*/_probe_*" until 2026-09-07; it was never true.) Its length is the NUMBER OF ASSERTIONS about the shipped bytes, and that number growing is the gate succeeding, not debt. The only real seam is the shipped-truth payload probe -- _shipped_truth_probe / run_shipped_truth_probe and the verdict functions reading their output, named rather than line-ranged because the old ~923-1386 was ~600 lines stale by 2026-09-07 -- which collects once and derives verdicts, because a per-check exec costs a container start — that is one subject with two probe strategies, not two subjects. Splitting it would mean the file a reader opens to answer "what do we actually assert about the shipped image?" is no longer one file. HISTORY: grew 2026-09-04: HT1 check_manifest_tree_arch — the manifest-driven ELF-machine audit that generalises check_flutter/check_rust_toolchain (docs/artifact-copy-completeness.md#the-shipped-trees-must-carry-the-images-own-arch); 2026-09-04: the HT1 tree-arch scanner reads candidates (executable/.so) before the rest and a capped walk is now a FAIL, not an INFO line; 2026-09-04: check_consumer_contract — the seven-row contract a consuming CI lane depends on and cannot repair from inside a read-only overlay layer, one probe plus five pure verdict functions (docs/consumer-image-contract.md#the-contract); 2026-09-04: the consumer-contract gate gained its JDK row (probe facts, verdict, symptom); +24 for the appimagetool contract row (probe fact, verdict, symptom); +47 on 2026-09-05: the cross-payload rule the tree-arch scanner needed, and the frozen-finding table (HT2); +2 on 2026-09-05 (lane llvm-host-libs) for emptying _RT_TREE_ARCH_FROZEN and pointing it at the doc -- the five llvm-target x86-64 libs it froze are fixed at the source now (HT3); +16 on 2026-09-05 (lane ht5-vulkan) for check_vulkan_loader reading which libvulkan actually answered and the whole-tree Vulkan probe (docs/artifact-copy-completeness.md#the-vulkan-tree-ships-only-what-the-image-runs); +47 on 2026-09-05 for check_vulkan_toolset -- the loader check proved libvulkan answers, nothing asserted the prefix carries tools you can build a shader with, and a library-only prefix shipped for months (docs/vulkan-foreign-arch-sdk.md); +104 on 2026-09-05 for check_android_abi -- /opt/android is tree-arch EXEMPT because an Android payload is never the image's own arch, so nothing could see that the ABI derived from the BUILD HOST and shipped x86_64 to every image; it reads .a members too, because the object that broke a consumer's link sat inside an archive (docs/linux-cross-builds.md#the-android-abi-is-a-target-not-the-build-host); +4 on 2026-09-05 to advertise and check WASM_PACK_VERSION and FLUTTER_RUST_BRIDGE_VERSION -- the ADV/HAVE row is also the proof that the two web-lane binaries are installed at their pins; +34 on 2026-09-05 for three contract rows that ask whether a thing is STAGED rather than writable (flatpak runtimes, the AppImage runtime, the two web-lane binaries) -- one shared verdict, and their cost stays written down once in _consumer_contract_symptom
